  "id": "dai",
  "term": "DAI",
  "definition": "DAI stands for dog-assisted interventions, also called dog-assisted services: organized activities or clinical applications that aim to support human wellbeing through interactions with dogs. In this context, the term also carries ethical concerns about protecting the dog’s welfare, individuality, and agency, with the handler’s skill and attention to the dog seen as central.",
